  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Stretch the pitch and cross",
  "description": "Six v six – five outfield players and a goalkeeper per team – on a pitch that is wider than it is long, for example 40 metres long and 50 metres wide. It is a normal game with one rule: a goal only counts if it comes straight from a cross or from a first-time pass after the cross.\n\nThe aim is for the team to always have one player out on each wing. Who goes wide changes during play – whoever leaves the wing to get into the box is replaced by a team-mate.\n\nVariation: three touches at most per player. You could also give two points for a goal from a cross when the team had players on both wings at once. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Get really wide – feet close to the touchline – when your team has the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Try to have a player on each wing at the same time so the opponents have to choose."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Run into the box as the cross is coming, not before: one to the near post, one to the far post."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Cross early when the space in front of goal is free."
    }
  ],
